Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:02.63,Cap,,0,0,0,,In nineteen\Neighty-three, deep
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.65,0:00:05.29,Cap,,0,0,0,,beneath an underground\Nbunker,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.31,0:00:07.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,an old man lay\Nstrapped to a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.79,0:00:10.55,Cap,,0,0,0,,metal table in total\Nsilence.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.57,0:00:12.88,Cap,,0,0,0,,Every sensory nerve in\Nhis body
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.90,0:00:15.01,Cap,,0,0,0,,had been surgically\Ncut.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.03,0:00:17.84,Cap,,0,0,0,,The scientists\Nbelieved that without
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.86,0:00:20.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,the five senses, human\Nthought could
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.70,0:00:23.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,reach the pure\Npresence of God.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.36,0:00:26.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,Instead, something far\Ndarker found him
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.84,0:00:30.03,Cap,,0,0,0,,in the void: hundreds\Nof dead voices
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.05,0:00:33.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,that refused to leave\Nhim alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.23,0:00:36.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,And before his heart\Nstopped forever,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.26,0:00:39.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,he delivered one final\Nmessage.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.02,0:00:41.10,Cap,,0,0,0,,Let us go back to the\Nbeginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.12,0:00:44.49,Cap,,0,0,0,,A team of deeply\Nreligious scientists
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.51,0:00:47.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,had theorized that\Nphysical senses
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.64,0:00:50.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,cloud our awareness of\Neternity.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.79,0:00:53.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,They believed that\Nwithout stimuli,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.26,0:00:55.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,a person could touch\Nthe divine.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.84,0:00:59.39,Cap,,0,0,0,,An elderly volunteer\Nwith nothing left to
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.41,0:01:03.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,live for agreed to the\Nradical surgery.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.02,0:01:05.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,Surgeons severed every\Nsensory nerve
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.99,0:01:09.11,Cap,,0,0,0,,connection leading\Ninto his brain.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.13,0:01:11.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,Although he retained\Nfull muscular
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.94,0:01:14.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,function, he was\Ncompletely
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.17,0:01:16.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,trapped inside his own\Nmind.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.71,0:01:20.05,Cap,,0,0,0,,Through one-way glass,\Nresearchers monitored
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.07,0:01:23.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,his slurred speech\Ninto a microphone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.22,0:01:25.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,On day four, he\Nwhispered that
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.62,0:01:28.07,Cap,,0,0,0,,he heard hushed,\Nunintelligible
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.09,0:01:29.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,voices in his head.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.82,0:01:32.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,Two days later, he\Nbegan to weep,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.59,0:01:34.59,Cap,,0,0,0,,crying out that his\Ndead
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.61,0:01:37.01,Cap,,0,0,0,,wife was speaking to\Nhim.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.03,0:01:40.28,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then, he began\Nreciting the private
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.30,0:01:43.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,names and secrets of\Nthe scientists'
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.67,0:01:45.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,own dead relatives.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.67,0:01:48.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,Terrified by what they\Nhad unsealed,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.60,0:01:50.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,half of the research\Nteam
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.64,0:01:53.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,fled the facility that\Nnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.32,0:01:56.39,Cap,,0,0,0,,Within a week, the\Nwhispers turned into a
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.41,0:01:59.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,deafening roar of\Nhundreds of spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.49,0:02:02.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,The man slammed\Nhimself against
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.26,0:02:05.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,walls seeking pain,\Nthen begged
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.02,0:02:07.37,Cap,,0,0,0,,for sedatives to\Nsleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.39,0:02:09.32,Cap,,0,0,0,,But in his dreams, he\Ncould
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.34,0:02:11.41,Cap,,0,0,0,,see the dead circling\Nhim.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.43,0:02:13.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,He clawed at his\Nuseless eyes,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.82,0:02:15.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,screaming that the\Nvoices
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.80,0:02:17.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,spoke only of hell.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.64,0:02:20.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,For five straight\Nhours, he shrieked:
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.74,0:02:23.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,No heaven, no\Nforgiveness!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.15,0:02:25.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,The scientists refused\Nto stop,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.72,0:02:27.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,convinced they were\Nmoments
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.96,0:02:30.33,Cap,,0,0,0,,away from contacting\NGod.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.35,0:02:33.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,Driven to absolute\Nmadness, he began
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.37,0:02:35.45,Cap,,0,0,0,,thrashing violently\Nuntil
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.47,0:02:38.19,Cap,,0,0,0,,researchers strapped\Nhim down.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.21,0:02:41.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,For two weeks, he\Nstared blankly
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.37,0:02:44.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,at the ceiling as\Nsilent tears
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.33,0:02:47.18,Cap,,0,0,0,,ran down his face,\Nkept alive
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.20,0:02:50.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,only by intravenous\Nfluids.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.18,0:02:53.29,Cap,,0,0,0,,On the fifteenth\Nnight, the blind man
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.31,0:02:55.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,slowly turned his head\Nand made
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.92,0:02:58.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,dead-center eye\Ncontact with the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.62,0:03:01.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,lead scientist through\Nthe glass.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.62,0:03:04.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,He whispered: I have\Nspoken with
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.11,0:03:06.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,God, and he has\Nabandoned us.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.58,0:03:08.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,In that exact second,\Nhis
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.59,0:03:10.66,Cap,,0,0,0,,heart stopped forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.68,0:03:13.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,Would you have severed\Nevery sensory
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.23,0:03:15.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,nerve to hear the\Nvoice of God?
